  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nIn both Chrome and Firefox, HTML &lt;area&gt; elements respect the `:hover` selector, allowing you to customize what cursor is shown on the clickable region they generate on the image. The `:active` selector, however, only applies in Chrome, not Firefox. From what I can tell, the spec doesn't define any of this.",
